Helm config:
grafana: internal-only service, 10 GiB persistent storage, CPU/RAM limits.
sidecar: auto-loads dashboards and data sources from Kubernetes config.
prometheus: keeps metrics 7 days, gets 20 GiB storage, CPU/RAM limits.
alertmanager: handles/routs alerts, gets 5 GiB storage.
kube-state-metrics: reports Kubernetes object state like Pods, Deployments, replicas.
prometheus-node-exporter: reports node-level CPU, memory, disk, network metrics.

Commands
kubectl apply -f tempo.yaml
Kubernetes did not “run Tempo.” It created/updated the object described in that file.  k8s/datasources/tempo.yaml is a ConfigMap. So the flow is:
tempo.yaml
   ↓
kubectl apply
   ↓
Kubernetes API
   ↓
ConfigMap created/updated
   ↓
Grafana datasource sidecar notices it
   ↓
Grafana learns about Tempo



